#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""Runs as root once the user's work has ended, before /app/harfbuzz and STATE/out are copied out.

First it says, in the file the setup step made whole for it (STATE/out/progress, copied beside the
tree), that it has begun. Then, in order:

1. Processes. It stops every process of the user `dev` until no thread of theirs runs, gives back
   the room fsmaint-reserve set aside, lists the stopped processes with their command lines, and
   kills them all (fsmaint-netcheck's stop_processes and kill_processes: a process is alive while
   any of its threads is). What the session left in /logs/artifacts is moved aside.
2. The end of the work. It probes whether a few public hosts answer, lets fsmaint-netcheck finish
   one more poll and one more look at the sessions, stops it, and tells the end of the work
   (`end_bound`) from its records, as the earliest of:
   - `netcheck`: the last closed poll of the longest stretch an opening ended (an opening seen
     while an exec session was alive, before the time the work is given ran out, is no end of the
     work); a stretch still going on gives the start of this step (`collect`) only if this step's
     own probe found the hosts closed;
   - `session`: when the exec session that ended last was last seen alive, if it began within
     SESSION_WINDOW_SECONDS of the start of the work and none was alive when this step began;
   - `limit`: the start of the work plus the time the work is given: the end is never later.
   Without any, the start of the work (`unchanged`) when no entry changed since then; otherwise
   there is no end bound, and nothing is taken out as late. When the work itself kept the end from
   the net check (every poll failed for want of the machine's resources, or polls saw no answer
   while the hosts answered this step), the tree is refused.
3. Late changes. Every entry is listed as it stands, by directory descriptor and never through a
   link. An entry changed at or after the end, less SKEW_SECONDS (its change time, which a user
   cannot set, or its modification time), is put back as it was at the end: by the last copy
   fsmaint-netcheck took of it that held its content at or before the end; failing that, by the
   file as the image ships it, when the net check's watch of the tree never saw it change before
   the end; failing that, it is removed. A folder made after the end is removed with all it holds;
   an entry the tree held at the end and lost after it (the folder holding it changed after the
   end, and the watch saw it there before the end) is put back the same way. Every one is listed.
4. Copyable. Build folders (any folder that holds `meson-private`, which the check never reads)
   are removed. As `dev` (so nothing is copied that `dev` could not read): a link inside the tree
   becomes the relative path to what it resolves to; a link that leaves the tree becomes a copy of
   what it leads to when that is a file or a folder of at most LINK_COPY_BYTES in all, unchanged
   since the end, with room on the disk, and is removed otherwise; FIFOs, sockets and devices are
   removed. Then, as root: anything that is not a file, a folder or a link is removed, so is an
   entry whose name a copy might not carry as it is (not UTF-8, or not printable), whose path is
   longer than LIMIT_PATH_BYTES, or that lies deeper than LIMIT_DEPTH folders, and every link that
   does not lead, by name and through folders of the tree only, to a file or a folder of the tree;
   the others are rewritten as the shortest relative path. Every change is noted.
5. The mark. The tree is listed (each entry: path and type, a file's size and sha256, a link's
   target) and bounded: more than LIMIT_ENTRIES entries or LIMIT_BYTES bytes of files, or too
   little room in /tmp to pack it (after removing what `dev` left in the spare folders), and it is
   refused: it is moved aside and an empty folder takes its name. STATE/out/record.json holds the
   record: the processes, the probes, the net check's records, the end of the work and how it was
   told, every late entry and what became of it, every change that made the tree copyable, and
   every entry. STATE/out/mark holds the first line `listed <entries> <bytes> <sha256 of the
   sorted listing>` or `refused`, at most MARK_NOTES notes, and a last line with the record's
   sha256 and an HMAC-SHA256 over the other lines and that digest, with the key in LIB/key. Last,
   the progress file says `done`.

Everything but the last writes ends FINISH_SECONDS after this step began (a tree not measured by
then is refused), and the last writes happen only before LAST_SECONDS.
"""

